10b. ROUND 9 (V6-m7; the owner's review of checkpoint 3, part 22, item A): THE THREE SINGLE FAILURES THE ROUND 8 TABLE MISSED, EACH
   STATED IN FULL. Round 9's first pass labelled them tolerated (L8P-D9); that label is WITHDRAWN: no requirement permits it
   THE REQUIREMENTS READ FOR A PERMITTED LATENT STATE (searched in their files, not recalled):
     v2/ecad/tools/pcb_requirements.yaml, 77 requirements: "latent", "proof test", "test interval", "diagnostic coverage": 0 matches
     REQ-044 "The cell block's protection does not rest on software alone ..." (the cell block's gauge and secondary)
     REQ-045 "From the cells to every load, the maximum fault current is bounded at each stage ..." (a protective element per stage, coordinated with
       what it protects): neither names a latent state, a detection interval or a coverage
     OPERATING-ENVELOPE section 4, "Single-fault conditions the design is expected to survive": the design's protections listed, no latent
       state admitted, and "No fault tree has been drawn and no coordination study exists" (PWR-003 open)
     C-PROT rev 1 (EXECUTION-PLAN.md): "every series part within its limits below and above the trip"
     the interval E-13b's "each service" rests on: NOT DEFINED (0 matches for a service or maintenance interval; the service life is TBD
       for prototype 1, OPERATING-ENVELOPE section 5). E-13b (a) is a technician's probe step (TP60 tied to TP63), run at commissioning
       and at a service: a docking or a power-up does not run it, so "at start" means once, at commissioning
     so NO approved requirement permits a latent state of the guard; each failure below is judged as a loss of required protection
   THE EXPOSURE WHILE THE GUARD IS LOST (RECORD l9stk 15.4, its protection output copied): the breaker's current limit 18.32 / 21.08 / 23.93 A
     (least / typical / most); without any guard the battery FETs reach 150 C held at 20.53 A from the 76.25 C air (21.38 A from +70 C),
     DERIVED, FETs only: a held current from 20.53 A to the breaker's own limit (up to 23.93 A) puts a series part over its limit BELOW THE
     TRIP, a condition C-PROT rev 1 covers; in the normal service of section 9 (a) (10 A held 89.4 C, the 18 A service 118.0 C, condition
     C4 121.8 C) no part is over its limit, with or without the guard
   (1) Q60's GATE SHORTED TO ITS DRAIN
     failed path: the gate network (R262 47 kOhm to OVERTEMP, low cold; R263 1.0 MOhm to ground) sits on the return; Q60 diode-connected
