       doubled), 17.8 uA through the network, against the 0.84 V the window needs: a ramping loop can be read held and a dead pack's
       precharge stopped (L4-E11 20c); tripped, the diode-connected Q60 conducts only above its own threshold (PRINTED 1.0 to 2.5 V at
       250 uA, 25 C), so it cannot be shown to pull the return under board P's first inverter's least 1.0 V: the trip is LOST
     detection still working: E-13b (a) only (TRIP_TEST fails to open the breaker). In service none: at the pack's least 10.6 V the return
       with the short reads 3.62 V (nominal parts), over the first inverter's 2.5 V: the loop reads closed and the kit runs
     the maximum interval before detection: to the next E-13b, UNBOUNDED (no service interval exists); the response until then: none
     the exposure in that interval: none in normal service; with a held current from 20.53 A to the breaker's limit the FETs pass 150 C,
       a prohibited temperature in a C-PROT rev 1 condition, NOT BOUNDED
     so a correction is required: 10c, the cold clamp (the short then trips)
   (2) C261 OPEN
     failed path: U61's only input capacitor
     function lost: TI SBVS186H 8.1.1, PRINTED: "An input capacitor is necessary if line transients greater than 10 V in magnitude are
       anticipated". A docking steps U61's input from 0 V to the closed DOCK_EN_OUT: 12.80 V at BRK_VIN 16.8 V, 22.48 V at the 29.2 V clamp,
       over 10 V from BRK_VIN 13.22 V (DERIVED, nominal parts): U61's response is then NOT PRINTED, so its output, both switches' VDD (6 V
       absolute), is not bounded during the step, and the guard's state after it is not printed
     detection: none in service and none in E-13b ((d) reads VDD's settled level, not a capacitor); the assembly's inspection only
     the maximum interval: UNBOUNDED (an open that develops in service, a cracked MLCC, is never looked for); the response: none
     the exposure: at each docking from BRK_VIN 13.22 V a voltage over the switch's 6 V absolute maximum cannot be excluded (a prohibited
       voltage condition, NOT BOUNDED); a switch it damages or leaves low is (1)'s exposure
     so a correction is required: 10c, C268 beside C261
   (3) U60's THERMAL PAD (pin 7) OPEN
     failed path: the die's main thermal path to the battery FETs' pour (pin 2 still grounds it electrically)
     function lost: the die couples through its six leads alone. Its own heating is 0.008 K with the pad and small without it, so a slow
       rise is followed; TI prints no thermal figure for the part without its pad, so the lag behind the pour in a rising overload is
       NOT BOUNDED and the trip may come after a battery FET passes 150 C (section 9 (b) leaves the junction's rise in the delay open too)
     detection: E-13's heat step at commissioning (the lag read through VTEMP at TP61) and an X-ray of the WSON at assembly; none in service
     the maximum interval: from commissioning, UNBOUNDED (a pad cracked in service by thermal fatigue is never looked for); response: none
     the exposure: a held current from 20.53 A to the breaker's limit, or a fast-rising overload: a FET over 150 C before the trip, NOT
       BOUNDED
     so a correction is required: 10c, a second switch U62 on its own pad, ORed
   A SECOND SHUNT ON THE SAME RETURN (round 9's first pass, recorded): its off leakage, 5.58 uA at 86.25 C, makes the sinks 24.41 uA on the
